        <children xmi:type="notation:Shape" xmi:id="_ZV7kwLkfEeSBQ7y8sEdlcw" type="Note" description="Illustration of the netwrok carrying exchanges. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;There is no added-value in this model in modelling the functional part of the transport over the network. Only network setup and configuration is modeled. &#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The transport between components are modeled with Physical Links. Here, the Physical Path &quot;Network Path&quot; is set to transport the Component Exchange &quot;Streaming Protocol&quot;, showing that all packets between &quot;Send&quot; and &quot;Split&quot; Functions as well as the stream Header actually go through the Ethernet network and switches. " fillColor="13369343" transparency="0" lineColor="6737151" lineWidth="1">
